cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Math Playground: interactive visualizations of classic mathematical results"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shahvaran
    given-names: Ali Reza
    email: ar.shahvaran@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/arshahvaran/math_playground"
url: "https://arshahvaran.github.io/math_playground/"
abstract: >-
  A browser-based application presenting six interactive probability
  simulations: a Galton board, the Maxwell-Boltzmann speed distribution,
  Buffon's needle, Monte Carlo pi, the arcsine law, and diffusion-limited
  aggregation. Every run is seeded and reproducible; five of the six converge
  to a value verifiable in closed form, and the sixth measures a fractal
  dimension that has none.
keywords:
  - mathematics
  - visualization
  - probability
  - central-limit-theorem
  - monte-carlo
  - kinetic-theory
  - chaos
  - interactive
  - education
  - webtool
